# Form State Retention Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
The problem is that several important forms wipe out their input fields (all data removes) when a user submits but a validation error occurs. This is caused by React/Next.js default form handling which can reset uncontrolled `<form action={...}>` inputs, or simply by DOM state loss upon server action failures re-rendering the view.

The goal is to fix this by transitioning all the critical forms to **Controlled Form Components** (binding input value directly to React `useState`). This explicit state binding prevents Next.js or React 19 from accidentally clearing input values and ensures all the data stays intact when an error is returned.

## Proposed Changes

We will implement a `formData` object mapped via `useState` and apply `value={formData.fieldName}` along with an `onChange` handler to all inputs inside the respective forms in **both** the `BCE` and `institute1` projects. 

